/*
** Separate as comma separated values for the configurations and follow the 
** same order as below.
** NAME                     - Specify the font name 
** POINT                    - Specify appropriate floating point value
** HEIGHT                   - Specify the font height as integer value  
** STYLE                    - Specify the font style as either Normal, Bold, Italic,Underline
**                            or strikeout
** PRERENDER                - Specify whether prerender should be enabled or not by setting 
**                            true or false
** USE_BGCOLOR              - Specify the useBgcolor as integer value
** CHAR_SPACING             - Specify the character spacing as integer value
** SPACE_CHAR_WIDTH         - Specify the space character width as integer value          
** KEYWORD_CUSTOM_FONT_PATH - Specify the font path if necessary 
** CHAR_SPACE_CTRL          - Specify whether the space control for characters should be
**                            enabled or not by giving a boolean value
** AA_MODE                  - Specify the mode as either 1BPP, 2BPP or 4BPP. 1BPPV Or 2BPPV if vertical
**                            packing is enabled    
** DEFAULT_CHAR             - Specify the default char to be displayed if the unicode range is not 
**                            specified within RANGE_START to RANGE_END 
** IMAGE_TO_CHAR            - Specify whether the image to char should be enabled or disabled by 
**                            setting true or false 
** IMG_PATH                 - Specify the image path or null as default
** KEYWORD_TEXT_RENDERING_HINT - Specify SingleBitPerPixelGridFit,AntiAlias,
**                          SingleBitPerPixel,AntiAliasGridFit,ClearTypeGridFit
**                          or SystemDefault
** SystemDefault            This will take the default settings of the PC 
** SingleBitPerPixelGridFit Each character is drawn using its glyph bitmap.
**                          Hinting is used to improve character appearance
**                          on stems and curvature.
** SingleBitPerPixel        Each character is drawn using its glyph bitmap.
**                          Hinting is not used.
** AntiAliasGridFit         Each character is drawn using its antialiased glyph
**                          bitmap with hinting. Much better quality due to
**                          antialiasing, but at a higher performance cost.This is not 
**                          applicable for 1bpp version of GDT.                                                 
** AntiAlias                Each character is drawn using its antialiased glyph
**                          bitmap without hinting. Better quality due to antialiasing.
**                          Stem width differences may be noticeable because hinting
**                          is turned off.This is not applicable for 1bpp version of GDT.
** ClearTypeGridFit         Each character is drawn using its glyph ClearType bitmap
**                          with hinting. The highest quality setting. Used to take
**                          advantage of ClearType font features. This is not 
**                          applicable for 1bpp version of GDT.
** KEYWORD_FONT_ENGINE         - Specify the font engine as Windows or Freetype2 
** KEYWORD_FREETYPE2_FONT_FILE - Specify the font file name or NULL as default
** KEYWORD_FREETYPE2_FONT_SIZE - Specify the font size required for Freetype2 
** KEYWORD_FREETYPE2_AUTO_HINT - Specify the auto hint as boolean value 
** KEYWORD_FONT_GROUP          - Specify whether to enable font group as a bool value
** KEYWORD_DEFAULT_INDEX       - Specify the default index
** KEYWORD_SELECTED_INDEX      - Specify the index to select 
** RANGE_START 
** Specify the valid range of unicodes 
** RANGE_END   
*/

